Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: png.c
Line: 609
Function: png_free_data
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: When freeing a single unknown chunk (num != -1), the code indexes info_ptr->unknown_chunks[num] without validating num against info_ptr->unknown_chunks_num. An out-of-range num results in out-of-bounds access and a png_free() on an out-of-bounds pointer, potentially corrupting the heap.

